The <eigenvector> equations $Q\mathbf e_i=\lambda_i\mathbf e_i$ combine column by column into $QE=ED$. Since $|E|\ne0$, multiplication by the <inverse matrix> gives the <diagonalization>
$$
\boxed{Q=EDE^{-1}}.
$$
The nonzero <determinant> of $E$ ensures that its columns form an <eigenbasis>.

= ii
{parent=c}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

Successive substitution in the <matrix> <recurrence relation> gives $V_k=V_0Q^k$. In the <matrix power> of $Q=EDE^{-1}$, every adjacent $E^{-1}E$ cancels, so $Q^k=ED^kE^{-1}$. Consequently
$$
\boxed{V_k=V_0ED^kE^{-1}},\qquad k\geq0.
$$
Here $D^k=\operatorname{diag}(\lambda_1^k,\ldots,\lambda_n^k)$ for $k\geq1$, and $D^0=I$. The formula also gives $V_0$ correctly at $k=0$.

